SUMMARY:Business Incubators
DESCRIPTION:Al-Qadisiyah University Business Incubator The Al-Qadisiyah University Business Incubator helps transform research and creative ideas into successful commercial ventures, and connects graduates with opportunities in industry and services.\nServices For students and graduates Entrepreneurship workshops and training Mentoring and support in developing business models Co-working spaces Seed funding for selected projects For startups 6–12 months of hosting and funding Mentoring from experts and specialised coaches Access to university laboratories and equipment A network of industrial partners Tracks Technology &amp; AI In partnership with the College of Computer Science and Information Technology.\nFood &amp; Agricultural Industries In partnership with the College of Agriculture and the College of Biotechnology.\nMedical &amp; Health Technologies In partnership with the colleges of Medicine, Pharmacy, and Dentistry.\nCreative Industries In partnership with the College of Fine Arts and the College of Arts.\nPartnerships Ministry of Higher Education — &ldquo;Ibtikar&rdquo; innovation programme Iraqi Federation of Industries International partners through exchange programmes Iraqi banks and funding institutions How to Apply Submit your idea via the online application form Attend an initial pitch session Evaluation by the incubator committee Selected projects are admitted Editor note: Add photos of the spaces, success-story examples, and update the application form link.\nRelated Innovation &amp; Entrepreneurship Jobs &amp; Careers Distinguished Alumni 
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
